    description: "FOUND by WI-tusad F3 (containment linker fix, corpus check). After the linker started rooting unplaced dotted names at their file, 5 dotted declarations on three samples stayed orphans because their file node's span does not enclose them: the Lua analyzer's file node in lua/moby/contrib/wireshark/memberlist.lua is named `file` with span 1-1 (the file has 587 lines; functions memberlist_protocol.dissector etc. at 122+), and purescript/ce2794/Lib.purs's file node spans 1-60 while its module spans 1-61. Invariant: a kind=\"file\" node's span covers every declaration in the file. Check every analyzer that mints its own file symbol (lua, purescript, others) against the orchestrator's file anchor."  # b2c1
